6. Basic Usage Guide

Recommended evaluation flow.

Access the web application using the deployed URL
Log in using the provided Google test account
Register personal availability on the calendar
View shared availability
Propose a group event by selecting a time slot
Accept or decline event invitations
Observe real time updates reflected immediately in the interface

A detailed, step by step user guide is provided in the separate User Manual PDF submission.

---

7. Backend and Data Information

ScheduleSync uses Firebase as its backend infrastructure.

Backend services used
Firebase Authentication
Firebase Firestore
Firebase Hosting

User schedules, event proposals, and responses are synchronized in real time using Firestore.

No sensitive credentials are included in this submission.
Only example configuration values are provided via `.env.example`.

---

8. Notes for Evaluators

This project is a prototype developed for an academic course submission.

The primary focus is on demonstrating social scheduling logic, real time synchronization, and user interaction flow rather than full production deployment.

For evaluation, use of the deployed web version is strongly recommended.

If any issues occur during access or evaluation, please refer to this README.install for guidance.

